# TipFacts — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env (never commit a real .env with real keys).

# Gemini API key used by POST /api/receipt/extract for VLM receipt-fact
# extraction. Required: without it the route returns 503 and the submit UI
# falls back to the manual track. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/
# (Bo: paste the real key into .env — this file stays a template).
#
# TIER (Bo, 2026-09-22): start on the FREE tier — prompts may be used for
# training, which is acceptable because only the already-redacted receipt
# image is ever sent. The route retries free-tier rate limits (429) with
# backoff, then falls back to the manual track. Switching to the paid tier
# later requires nothing more than swapping in a paid-tier key here — the
# code deliberately avoids paid-tier-only features (no batch API, no
# context caching).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Gemini model used for extraction. Defaults to gemini-3-flash-preview when
# unset (with gemini-3.6-flash as the code-level fallback).
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3-flash-preview

# Optional fallback provider for receipt extraction (OpenAI-compatible).
# When the whole Gemini chain fails (or no Gemini key is set), the route
# tries this endpoint with the same prompt and validation. Defaults are the
# OpenRouter free Qwen VL tier — get a free key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
# (no card required). Free-tier note: assume prompts may be used for
# training; acceptable because only the already-redacted image is ever sent.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=qwen/qwen2.5-vl-32b-instruct:free
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Max submissions per IP per hour. Default 20 when unset — generous enough for
# real testing, still a backstop against floods.
# SUBMIT_RATE_LIMIT=20
